      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:50:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done\n\n\u003e If guest page size could vary, why is it a constant?\n\nYes, that\u0027s a fair point.\n\npvmfw needs to satisfy page-alignment requirements from the guest kernel (e.g. for the BCC region) so having `GUEST_PAGE_SIZE` in the code instead of a plain `PAGE_SIZE` or `SIZE_4K` allows us to easily grep through the code and locate which \"constants\" would need to be modified to support guests using larger granules. Until then, it\u0027s just a constant.",
      "parentUuid": "31552571_61bf7554",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "843ceb9c50c150a3ae46c701949c4cb926051bd1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
